					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-680780#post-1830483</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-680780/and-the-winner-is#post-1830483</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 11 Aug 2013 08:43:01 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Smapti</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>362048</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>All the &quot;errors&quot; in the last segment are intentional. By this point, Anderson has rewritten history over and over so many times that the time-space continuum is essentially broken - thus why it's winter and summer at the same time, the courier is wearing a Hawaiian shirt and banging a gong to announce himself, the doctor has a bed in his office, etc.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-680780#post-1830348</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-680780/and-the-winner-is#post-1830348</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 11 Aug 2013 00:28:49 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Lennartsson</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1455404</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Alright, makes sense.</p> <p>Though I have to point out something at the last part. It says:</p> <blockquote> <p>Dr. James Anderson woke up in his office and climbed out of bed. It was a sunny <strong>Sunday</strong> afternoon and lunch break was over&#8230;</p> </blockquote> <p>While at the end of it it says:</p> <blockquote> <p>Anderson yawned as his alarm clock went off - 37:65 on <strong>Marsday</strong>, Quatuordecimber 72nd.</p> </blockquote> <p>Was it intentional to have it say Sunday just to make it seem less obvious that this is a timeline that measures time in a different way, until the very end?</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-680780#post-1830128</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-680780/and-the-winner-is#post-1830128</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 10 Aug 2013 14:23:56 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Drewbear</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>301632</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>The article for the SCP that he uses to send his messages back in time (the &quot;first&quot; time, anyway), implies that it's retroactively altering the core timeline rather than creating split timelines.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
